and never copy a path from it into a committed page.
-->
# Machine-local context — not committed

**Host:** `<output of hostname>`
If `hostname` does not print exactly this, the file was copied from another
machine: ignore every path below and ask before writing anything.

## Role

Writer. Pull first (`git pull --rebase`) before a session's first write; one
writing session at a time across machines.

## Absolute paths on THIS machine

- this KB:            `<absolute path to this clone>`
- raw store (opt.):   `<KB_RAW_STORE folder, or "local raw/ folders">`
- sibling KB (opt.):  `<absolute path to a club/lab/startup KB, or delete this line>`

## Modules enabled on this machine (optional)

List each installed module and WHERE its machine-local config lives, never
the values (no tokens, no passwords, no mailbox contents).

- `<module name>`: `<config location, e.g. "~/.config/canvas/env (mode 600)">`
- `<module name>`: `<e.g. "Thunderbird profile auto-detected" or an env var name>`

## Course workspaces (optional)

Local folders outside the repo that hold course files you do not commit
(lecture slides, past exams, practice sets). Skills such as exam-prep read
them in place and cite files by name.

- `<COURSE CODE>`: `<absolute path to that course's local folder>`

## Local quirks (optional)

- `<anything an agent must know on this machine, e.g. which shell to use>`
